// The contract for the live-path comparison: the smallest thing that is still the workload.
// One publisher changes a value at a fixed rate and N subscribers must each see every change.
//
// One property and not two, deliberately. QtRO coalesces outbound property changes, so a
// stamp pushed beside a payload can arrive in either order or merged, and the measurement
// would be of the coalescing rather than of the path. The frame carries its own stamp
// instead: the first 8 bytes are microseconds since the run began, the rest is the payload.
// That is also exactly what the Node side puts on the wire, so the two columns are timing
// the same interval in the same way and differ only in the protocol carrying it.
class LiveFeed
{
    PROP(QByteArray frame READPUSH)
}
